From: Paul Praschl <praschlpaul@g-p.at>
Date: Mon, 3 Aug 2026 12:45:07 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 096/117] iio: light: tsl2583: Add Apple CT821 support

Apple CT821 sensors use a TSL2581-compatible register map with a distinct
gain register and initialization sequence. Add match data, the CT821-only
attribute group, and the required register programming while preserving
the generic TSL258x path.

Read the per-device LSCI factory record through NVMEM and use its
integration, gain, dark-count, coefficient, and aperture factors for lux
conversion. Validate the record, reject zero or overflowing recursive
gain factors before narrowing them, guard every divisor, and saturate
overflowing lux arithmetic.

Treat gain and integration-time changes as transactions. Restore both the
previous software settings and hardware configuration after an I2C
failure. If restoration also fails, mark the device for full
reinitialization, power it down, and synchronize runtime PM so the next
access starts from a defined state.

Signed-off-by: Paul Praschl <praschlpaul@g-p.at>
[Orchard: ported to v7.3-rc1: mainline removed tsl2583_set_pm_runtime_busy() in favour of direct pm_runtime_resume_and_get()/pm_runtime_put_autosuspend() calls; tsl2583_put_pm_after_error() and the CT821 paths use those directly]

Orchard-replay-of: 4ef53b25e2938fb9d5de31bbb659b6a04fe923a8
